# Simulation Results

## 1. Overview

The Triple Modular Redundancy (TMR) system was simulated using Verilog HDL in an online simulator. The simulation verifies the functionality of three redundant 8-bit adders, the majority voter, and the fault detection mechanism.

## 2. Test Cases

| Test Case | Input A | Input B | Fault Injection | Output | Fault Detected |
|---|---:|---:|---|---:|---|
| Normal Operation | 5 | 3 | Disabled | 8 | No |
| Fault Injection | 10 | 20 | Enabled | 30 | Yes |
| Maximum Carry | 255 | 1 | Disabled | 256 | No |

## 3. Observations

- The system produces the correct output during normal operation.
- A single injected fault in the third adder is masked by the majority voter.
- The fault detection logic identifies the faulty module.
- The 9-bit output preserves the carry generated during maximum 8-bit addition.

## 4. Conclusion

The simulation verifies that the designed TMR system can tolerate a single injected fault in one of its redundant modules while maintaining the correct output. The design demonstrates the application of digital redundancy and majority voting for fault-tolerant digital systems.
